{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>When He struck Egypt.</b> On the night of the fifteenth of Nisan." "<b>And our houses He delivered.</b> In remembrance of that miracle we perform this commandment. Another interpretation: <b>What is this service to you?</b> — that we eat it roasted, for no other consecrated flesh is eaten roasted." "<b>And you shall say: it is the pesach sacrifice.</b> And because it is a sacrifice of haste, we eat it roasted, for that is the way of haste. <b>And the people bowed and prostrated themselves.</b> This is acceptance of the commandment — they accepted upon themselves to do all that was stated above. For so is the way of everyone who accepts to do what he is commanded: he bows his neck, and in his prostration it is seen that he has accepted the commandment upon himself."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:22.620769169Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}